# cross-lib-activity-missing — Lib A (the referring policy library).
library "Root".

// Root's decision recommends `"Shared"."Nonexistent Activity"`. The Shared
// library exists and is pulled into the closure, but has no activity by that
// name, so the FHIR activityResolver's `index.activities.get("Shared")?.has(...)`
// guard misses → the resolver returns null (fail-closed) rather than fabricating
// a recommendation URL. That surfaces as an `unresolved-activity` UnmatchedReference
// which cascades the decision to `decision-cascade-suppressed`; the emit does NOT
// silently succeed.

concept "Active Crohns Disease":
- type is Condition.
- value type is boolean.
- code is `active-crohns-disease`.

decision "Triage Crohns":
- when "Active Crohns Disease" then recommend activity "Shared"."Nonexistent Activity".
